      {
        "title": "Show HN: Pi pod – Run your pi coding agent in sandboxes on your own server",
        "link": "https://pipod.dev/",
        "description": "<p>pi pod runs sessions of the pi coding agent in isolated sandboxes (\"pods\") on a server you run, in composable environments.<p>----<p>Since moving my company towards AI-native work, I have been really frustrated by the state of \"agentic engineering\" environments. Products by the labs (claude code, codex) lock you into a single provider for your tokens. Agnostic solutions (factory, devin, arguably cursor) make you pay per-token costs. None of these products allow you to fully customize the harness, and of course they all run on someone else's infrastructure.<p>I've been an early and fervent user of pi, which I think is fantastically simple and beautiful software. I have felt it needs an environment for it to work across platforms with fully functional composability for teams.<p>This is very much a work in progress, but for my team this has been a much needed solution and has helped us tremendously. I hope you will give it a try and let me know how you would like it to improve.</p>\n<hr>\n<p>Comments URL: <a href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=49937304\">https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=49937304</a></p>\n<p>Points: 38</p>\n<p># Comments: 22</p>",
        "pubDate": "Fri, 02 Oct 2026 19:10:38 +0000",
        "guid": "https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=49937304"
      },
